1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,432
Yesterday's fix can break today's system.

2
00:00:02,432 --> 00:00:10,537
Ripple is an evidence-driven incident recovery agent: it follows connected evidence, challenges an outdated recommendation, and verifies what actually works.

3
00:00:13,581 --> 00:00:18,901
This is the latest Ripple interface, replaying actual Gemini output against FalkorDB Cloud.

4
00:00:18,901 --> 00:00:23,812
Six synthetic services connect dependencies, owners, deployments, source records, and action constraints.

5
00:00:23,812 --> 00:00:26,677
The paths shown here came from FalkorDB.

6
00:00:28,192 --> 00:00:30,376
Checkout failures follow a payments release.

7
00:00:30,376 --> 00:00:34,744
An earlier compatibility record permits rollback, and the agent initially proposes it.

8
00:00:34,744 --> 00:00:39,113
The timeline preserves that recommendation and the evidence available at the time.

9
00:00:40,209 --> 00:00:42,601
Then a ledger migration changes the facts.

10
00:00:42,601 --> 00:00:45,676
The old deployment is incompatible with the current schema.

11
00:00:45,676 --> 00:00:51,485
Ripple marks the earlier proposal stale, and the actual sequence driver confirms that its approval cannot execute.

12
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:58,325
The original migration source blocks rollback while permitting a feature flag change.

13
00:00:58,325 --> 00:01:00,771
Source provenance makes this constraint inspectable.

14
00:01:00,771 --> 00:01:03,625
The replacement recommendation must cite retrieved evidence.

15
00:01:04,749 --> 00:01:07,694
The agent recommends disabling strict currency validation.

16
00:01:07,694 --> 00:01:12,322
Deterministic code rechecks the revision and executes the approved simulator action.

17
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:16,950
Checkout, payments, and storefront each change from HTTP 503 to 200.

18
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:19,054
Only then is recovery verified.

19
00:01:20,935 --> 00:01:26,130
A fresh investigation retrieves and explicitly cites the previous model-selected, probe-verified recovery from FalkorDB.

20
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:28,727
Earlier chat messages are not carried over.

21
00:01:28,727 --> 00:01:33,551
Current constraints still have to match before that memory can justify another action.

22
00:01:35,099 --> 00:01:39,858
In the third scenario, the available records do not justify a supported remediation.

23
00:01:39,858 --> 00:01:42,786
Ripple identifies the missing diagnostics and executes nothing.

24
00:01:42,786 --> 00:01:47,545
Failed and uncertain outcomes remain visible; they are never stored as successful procedures.

25
00:01:48,792 --> 00:01:54,758
A separate hosted HTTP test verified recovery with one Gemini call and a 7.014-second investigation.

26
00:01:54,758 --> 00:02:01,123
Duplicate approval returned the same result, memory survived scenario reload, and another visitor received a 404.

27
00:02:01,123 --> 00:02:03,112
The raw receipt is public.

28
00:02:05,146 --> 00:02:11,704
In a separate CPU-model benchmark, graph mode met twelve of twelve expected outcomes; full-document context met eleven.

29
00:02:11,704 --> 00:02:15,176
Graph mode was slower and missed complete impact twice.

30
00:02:15,176 --> 00:02:17,877
All twenty-four records, including failures, are published.

31
00:02:17,877 --> 00:02:20,191
This is not a Gemini comparison.

32
00:02:21,356 --> 00:02:23,383
Three consecutive CPU sequences passed.

33
00:02:23,383 --> 00:02:30,677
One complete native Gemini sequence passed; three consecutive native sequences remain unverified, and the free quota is exhausted.

34
00:02:30,677 --> 00:02:32,298
These are synthetic incidents.

35
00:02:32,298 --> 00:02:35,135
The approved demo database connection is plaintext.

36
00:02:35,135 --> 00:02:37,161
No production systems are connected.

37
00:02:37,735 --> 00:02:42,822
Ripple makes the decision inspectable, the action guarded, and the outcome measurable.

38
00:02:42,822 --> 00:02:49,180
Explore the latest console, inspect the public proof, and reproduce the project from its source.

39
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:50,876
Built with AI assistance.
